# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every text file is stored LF in the repository and checked out CRLF on
# Windows. Without this, the storage form was whatever the file happened to
# have when it was first added -- in practice CRLF -- and any editor that
# wrote LF turned its next commit into a whole-file rewrite. main.tex did
# exactly that on 2026-08-09: 987 insertions and 1026 deletions, of which 65
# lines were real, which is enough noise to hide someone's actual change.
#
# The checkout side is left to each machine. Until 2026-11-02 this line read
# `text=auto eol=crlf`, and `eol=crlf` is not "CRLF on Windows": it forces CRLF
# on every platform, so a Linux or macOS checkout got CRLF too and the
# `#!/usr/bin/env python3` line of tools/audit.py ended in a carriage return,
# which the kernel then looks for as part of the interpreter's name. With
# `text=auto` alone, git converts to core.eol on checkout, which defaults to
# `native`: CRLF on Windows, LF everywhere else. Storage in the repository
# stays LF either way, so this changes no committed file.
*               text=auto

# Scripts run through a shebang need LF on every platform, Windows included
# (Git Bash and WSL read the same files). Python itself accepts either.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries -- never touch these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# main.pdf is tracked (see .gitignore), so a mistaken text conversion would
# corrupt the deliverable. Git's auto-detection has caught it so far; saying
# it outright removes the dependency on that.
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gz            binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Diff behaviour
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Gives \chapter, \section and friends as hunk headers in git diff output.
*.tex           diff=tex
